   "t": 1791259879.5403259,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "The stop trigger fired as declared (in-sample Sharpe 1.2623 > 1.2 bar). I've used exactly 3 content moves (init, extend_best, extend_best), each adding meaningful improvement with no failures along the way \u2014 a clean, consistent search path.\n\nNow let me think about the out-of-sample prediction. A few considerations:\n- In-sample Sharpe of 1.2623 was achieved with only 3 greedy moves out of 40 features \u2014 low risk of overfitting compared to an exhaustive search over many combinations.\n- Each step showed a solid, monotonic gain (0.95 \u2192 1.18 \u2192 1.26), suggesting genuine signal rather than noise-chasing.\n- Still, in-sample Sharpes on daily equity-like panels typically overstate out-of-sample performance due to selection effects (even picking the \"best single feature\" from 40 candidates involves a multiple-comparisons haircut), and costs/turnover can behave differently out-of-sample.\n- A reasonable discount is on the order of 30-45% of in-sample Sharpe, with meaningful uncertainty.\n\nI'll predict a mean notably below the in-sample value, with a wide standard deviation reflecting genuine uncertainty."
